---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Project Three" description="A portfolio experience built from Astroplate visuals, without Astroplate bloat.">
  <section class="max-w-2xl">
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm tracking-wide text-text-light">
      <a href="/projects" class="hover:text-primary">← Projects</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-black text-text-dark md:text-5xl">Project Three</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-text-light">A portfolio experience built from Astroplate visuals, without Astroplate bloat.</p>

    <img
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504639725590-34d0984388bd?w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80"
      alt="Project Three"
      width="1200"
      height="630"
      class="mb-10 w-full rounded-lg object-cover"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      Project Three started as an experiment: take the visual language of Astroplate and rebuild it from first
      principles, keeping only what actually earns its place. The outcome is a portfolio template that looks polished
      without the weight of a full-featured starter.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      Unnecessary abstractions were stripped out — no content collections, no i18n layer, no search index. What
      remained is a clean base that's easy to read, extend, and hand off.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">What I built</h2>
    <p class="mb-4 text-text-light">
      A focused component library covering layout, navigation, cards, and typography — each component doing one thing
      well. The design tokens live in a single Tailwind config file, making a full visual rebrand a one-file change.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-10 text-text-light">
      The mobile experience was a first-class concern throughout: touch targets, font scaling, and layout all tested
      on real devices before shipping, not as an afterthought.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl text-text-dark">Tech stack</h2>
    <ul class="mb-10 list-disc pl-5 text-text-light space-y-1">
      <li>Astro</li>
      <li>Tailwind CSS</li>
      <li>TypeScript</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
